{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f5e9d746-4571-4d7c-a0e1-4f9ac6440c26","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A vector represents a displacement: its length gives the size, and its arrow gives the direction. Start with vector a.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Adding vectors head to tail"},{"op":"figure","id":"vectors","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.7,5.7],"y":[-0.8,4.2],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"start","at":[0,0],"label":"O"},{"kind":"segment","id":"veca","from":{"at":"start"},"to":[3,0],"arrow":true,"label":"a"},{"kind":"point","id":"joint","at":{"on":"veca","t":1}}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f5e9d746-4571-4d7c-a0e1-4f9ac6440c26","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Place the tail of vector b at the head of a. You may slide b, but keep its length and direction unchanged.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"addb","on":"vectors","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"vecb","from":{"at":"joint"},"to":[5,3],"arrow":true,"label":"b"},{"kind":"point","id":"finish","at":{"on":"vecb","t":1},"label":"P"}]},{"op":"text","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.12},"content":"Slide, do not rotate."}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f5e9d746-4571-4d7c-a0e1-4f9ac6440c26","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The sum is one arrow from the original tail to the final head. It produces the same displacement as following a, then b.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"resultant","on":"vectors","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"sumarrow","from":{"at":"start"},"to":{"at":"finish"},"arrow":true,"label":"a + b"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"sumlaw","anchor":{"el":"rule","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\vec{R}=\\vec{a}+\\vec{b}=\\overrightarrow{OP}"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Where should the resultant arrow start and end?","expected_gist":"It starts at the tail of a, O, and ends at the head of b, P."}}}
